CRASH-15: reject an external-buildup time series index that does not exist

For an EXTERNAL buildup function, coefficient 3 is the index of the
loading time series, and landuse_getExternalBuildup() reads
Tseries[(int)floor(coeff[2])] at every runoff step. setLanduseValue()
accepted any coefficient 3 >= 0 and any function code, so an EXTERNAL
function could be given, or switched to, an index past the end of Tseries[]
(an out-of-bounds read, or a crash with no time series at all) or a value
too large for an int (undefined conversion). Return ERR_API_PROPERTY_VALUE
when the setter would leave an EXTERNAL function with coefficient 3 not
below the number of time series.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-15_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
index 4096c9a..733c91a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/swmm5.c
@@ -1817,6 +1817,10 @@ int setLanduseValue(int property, int index, int subIndex, double value)
     switch (property)
     {
     case swmm_LANDUSE_BUILDUP_FUNC:
+        // --- coefficient 3 of an external function is a time series index
+        if ((int)value == EXTERNAL_BUILDUP &&
+            Landuse[index].buildupFunc[subIndex].coeff[2] >= Nobjects[TSERIES])
+            return ERR_API_PROPERTY_VALUE;
         Landuse[index].buildupFunc[subIndex].funcType = (int)value;
         recomputeBuildupMaxDays(index, subIndex);
         return 0;
@@ -1832,6 +1836,9 @@ int setLanduseValue(int property, int index, int subIndex, double value)
         return 0;
     case swmm_LANDUSE_BUILDUP_COEFF3:
         if (value < 0.0) return ERR_API_PROPERTY_VALUE;
+        if (Landuse[index].buildupFunc[subIndex].funcType == EXTERNAL_BUILDUP &&
+            value >= Nobjects[TSERIES])
+            return ERR_API_PROPERTY_VALUE;
         Landuse[index].buildupFunc[subIndex].coeff[2] = value;
         recomputeBuildupMaxDays(index, subIndex);
         return 0;
